sequenceDiagram
    participant ML as ML Application
    participant Route as OpenShift Route<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant FS as Feature Server (Python)<br/>6566/TCP HTTP/HTTPS
    participant Store as Online Store<br/>(Redis/PostgreSQL)
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Operator as Feast Operator<br/>(controller-runtime)
    participant S3 as S3 Storage<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over ML,Store: Flow 1: Online Feature Retrieval
    ML->>Route: POST /get-online-features<br/>Auth: Kubernetes RBAC / OIDC / None
    Route->>FS: Forward (Edge/Reencrypt TLS)
    FS->>Store: Read features<br/>Auth: Store credentials
    Store-->>FS: Feature values
    FS-->>Route: JSON Response
    Route-->>ML: Feature response

    Note over K8sAPI,Operator: Flow 2: FeatureStore CR Reconciliation
    K8sAPI->>Operator: Watch event: FeatureStore CR<br/>TLS 1.2+, ServiceAccount token
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Create/Update Deployment<br/>TLS 1.2+, ServiceAccount token
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Create/Update Service, Route, RBAC<br/>TLS 1.2+, ServiceAccount token
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Create ServiceMonitor, HPA, PDB<br/>TLS 1.2+, ServiceAccount token

    Note over Operator,K8sAPI: Flow 3: Notebook Integration
    K8sAPI->>Operator: Watch event: Notebook CR + FeatureStore CR<br/>TLS 1.2+
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Create/Update ConfigMap<br/>(feature_store.yaml for notebook)<br/>TLS 1.2+

    Note over FS,S3: Flow 4: Materialization
    FS->>Store: Write materialized features<br/>Auth: Store credentials
    FS->>S3: Read offline data<br/>Auth: AWS IAM / configured
    S3-->>FS: Source data
    FS->>Store: Write online features
